# Headings: a heading with several Text inside and its own Box and Typography.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Headings · Several texts
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: chapter
			Box:
				Margin: 10 0 12 0
				Padding: 12 14
				Border: 0 0 0 4
				Border color: accent
				Background: tint
		For style: kicker
			Typography:
				Size: 8
				Line height: 12
				Weight: 600
				Color: muted
				Case: uppercase
				Letter spacing: 1
		For style: subtitle
			Typography:
				Size: 10
				Line height: 14
				Bold: false
				Italic: true
				Color: muted
	Section:
		Text: Headings
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Several texts
		Paragraph: A heading is a block with one or more `Text` inside, which inherit its `Typography`. Here a `Heading 2` holds a small kicker, the title and a subtitle, each a `Text` with its own style, and its `Box` gives it a strip and a background.
			Style: intro
		Heading 2:
			Style: chapter
			Typography:
				Size: 18
				Line height: 22
				Bold: true
			Text: Chapter 3
				Style: kicker
			Text: The valley in autumn
			Text: Walks, markets and the chestnut fair
				Style: subtitle
		Paragraph: The PDF bookmark and the table of contents take the texts of the heading in order.
